# Completeness of the Renes-Costello-Batina addition on secp256k1: for P and
# Q on the curve with y1 and y2 nonzero (on this curve a point is (0, 0, 0)
# exactly when its y is 0: a point with y == 0 has x^3 == -7 z^3, and -7 is
# not a cube), the Y of P + Q is nonzero. The proof: W Y3 == N^3 + 7 D^3
# (C.compl_y), so Y3 == 0 forces D == 0 and N == 0, then
# s^3 + 7 (2 z1 z2)^3 == 0 (C.compl_s) forces z1 z2 == 0; and with P (or Q)
# at infinity Y3 == y1^2 y2^2 (C.inf_y).
#
# The hypotheses on the modulus m = 1 + mp: m is prime (hp), 3 divides
# m - 1 (h3), (-7)^((m-1)/3) != 1 (hnc), 21 < m (h21).

